## 9. Transfers and Escalation

A patient may move during admission without closing the IPD encounter. ICU and theater transfers use dedicated overlay flows.


| Transfer Type         | Example                                      | Flow reference |
| --------------------- | -------------------------------------------- | -------------- |
| Bed transfer          | Same ward, different bed.                    | IPD bed board Â§14.2 |
| Ward transfer         | Medical ward to surgical ward.               | IPD `request-transfer` |
| ICU transfer          | Ward to ICU or ICU to step-down ward.        | [icu-flow Â§11](./icu-flow.mdc) |
| Isolation transfer    | Move due to infection control need.          | IPD transfer |
| OT/procedure transfer | Temporary movement for surgery or procedure. | [theater-flow Â§7](./theater-flow.mdc) |
| External transfer     | Referral or transfer to another hospital.    | IPD encounter outcome |


Each transfer should record reason, from-location, to-location, requested by, approved by, transfer time, handover note, and billing impact.

